msgid "Dev UI"
msgstr ""

msgid "Dev UI v1"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This guide covers the Dev UI v1, which has been replaced in Quarkus 3 with "
"xref:dev-ui-v2.adoc[a new Dev UI].\n"
"You can still access the Dev UI v1 using http://localhost:8080/q/dev-v1[/q/"
"dev-v1]"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This guide covers the Quarkus Dev UI for xref:building-my-first-extension."
"adoc[extension authors]."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Quarkus ships with a new experimental Dev UI, which is available in dev mode "
"(when you start\n"
"quarkus with `mvn quarkus:dev`) at http://localhost:8080/q/dev-v1[/q/dev-v1] "
"by default. It will show you something like\n"
"this:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"It allows you to quickly visualize all the extensions currently loaded, see "
"their status and go directly\n"
"to their documentation."
msgstr ""

msgid "On top of that, each extension can add:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"xref:how-can-i-make-my-extension-support-the-dev-ui[Custom useful bits of "
"runtime information in the overview]"
msgstr ""

msgid "xref:adding-full-pages[Full custom pages]"
msgstr ""

msgid "xref:advanced-usage-adding-actions[Interactive pages with actions]"
msgstr ""

msgid "How can I make my extension support the Dev UI?"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In order to make your extension listed in the Dev UI you don't need to do "
"anything!"
msgstr ""

msgid "So you can always start with that :)"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If you want to contribute badges or links in your extension card on the Dev "
"UI overview\n"
"page, like this:"
msgstr ""

msgid "image:dev-ui-embedded.png[alt=Dev UI embedded,role=\"center\"]"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You have to add a file named `dev-templates/embedded.html` in your\n"
"xref:building-my-first-extension.adoc#description-of-a-quarkus-"
"extension[`deployment`]\n"
"extension module's resources:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The contents of this file will be included in your extension card, so for "
"example we can place\n"
"two links with some styling and icons:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Note how the paths are specified: `{config:http-path('quarkus.smallrye-"
"openapi.path')}`. This is a special\n"
"directive that the quarkus dev console understands: it will replace that "
"value with the resolved route\n"
"named 'quarkus.smallrye-openapi.path'."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The corresponding non-application endpoint is declared using `."
"routeConfigKey` to associate the route with a name:"
msgstr ""

msgid "The configured path is resolved into a valid route."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The resolved route path is then associated with the key `quarkus.smallrye-"
"openapi.path`."
msgstr ""

msgid "Path considerations"
msgstr ""

msgid "Paths are tricky business. Keep the following in mind:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Assume your UI will be nested under the dev endpoint. Do not provide a way "
"to customize this without a strong reason."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Never construct your own absolute paths. Adding a suffix to a known, "
"normalized and resolved path is fine."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Configured paths, like the `dev` endpoint used by the console or the "
"SmallRye OpenAPI path shown in the example above,\n"
"need to be properly resolved against both `quarkus.http.root-path` and "
"`quarkus.http.non-application-root-path`.\n"
"Use `NonApplicationRootPathBuildItem` or `HttpRootPathBuildItem` to "
"construct endpoint routes and identify resolved\n"
"path values that can then be used in templates."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The `{devRootAppend}` variable can also be used in templates to construct "
"URLs for static dev console resources, for example:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Refer to the xref:all-config.adoc#quarkus-vertx-http_quarkus-http-non-"
"application-root-path[Quarkus Vertx HTTP configuration reference]\n"
"for details on how the non-application root path is configured."
msgstr ""

msgid "Template and styling support"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Both the `embedded.html` files and any full page you add in `/dev-templates` "
"will be interpreted by\n"
"xref:qute.adoc[the Qute template engine]."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This also means that you can xref:qute-reference.adoc#user_tags[add custom "
"Qute tags] in\n"
"`/dev-templates/tags` for your templates to use."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The style system currently in use is https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.6/"
"getting-started/introduction/[Bootstrap V4 (4.6.0)]\n"
"but note that this might change in the future."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The main template also includes https://jquery.com/[jQuery 3.5.1], but here "
"again this might change."
msgstr ""

msgid "Accessing Config Properties"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A `config:property(name)` expression can be used to output the config value "
"for the given property name.\n"
"The property name can be either a string literal or obtained dynamically by "
"another expression.\n"
"For example `{config:property('quarkus.lambda.handler')}` and `{config:"
"property(foo.propertyName)}`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Reminder: do not use this to retrieve raw configured path values. As shown "
"above, use `{config:http-path(...)}` with\n"
"a known route configuration key when working with resource paths."
msgstr ""

msgid "Adding full pages"
msgstr ""

msgid "To add full pages for your Dev UI extension such as this one:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You need to place them in your extension's\n"
"xref:building-my-first-extension.adoc#description-of-a-quarkus-"
"extension[`deployment`] module's\n"
"`/dev-templates` resource folder, like this page for the xref:cache."
"adoc[`quarkus-cache` extension]:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In order to benefit from the same style as other Dev UI pages, extend the "
"`main` template"
msgstr ""

msgid "You can pass extra CSS for your page in the `style` template parameter"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can pass extra JavaScript for your page in the `script` template "
"parameter. This will be added inline after the JQuery script, so you can "
"safely use JQuery in your script."
msgstr ""

msgid "Don't forget to set your page title in the `title` template parameter"
msgstr ""

msgid "The `body` template parameter will contain your content"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In order for your template to read custom information from your Quarkus "
"extension, you can use\n"
"the `info` xref:qute-reference.adoc#namespace_extension_methods[namespace]."
msgstr ""

